CRASH-03: reject a PRIORITY clause that has no value

newpriority() passed Tok[1] to getfloat() without checking the token
count. For a bare PRIORITY line Tok[1] is NULL, so strtod() read
address 0 and EPANET crashed, from EN_open and from EN_addrule. The
clause is now a syntax error (201), which EN_open reports as error 200
and EN_addrule returns as 250.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply CRASH-03_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/rules.c b/src/rules.c
index 1b009ad..35e9fe7 100644
--- a/src/rules.c
+++ b/src/rules.c
@@ -940,6 +940,7 @@ int newpriority(Project *pr)
     double x;
     char **Tok = pr->parser.Tok;
 
+    if (pr->parser.Ntokens < 2) return 201;
     if (!getfloat(Tok[1], &x)) return 202;
     net->Rule[net->Nrules].priority = x;
     return 0;
